{"id":156757177976479,"type":"album","name":"Club Classics Vol. One","artist":"Soul II Soul","year":1989,"weight":12,"info":{"cover":"https://dn711104.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-122b6782-e9e3-3ea3-9947-1dc6ab6946ce/mbid-122b6782-e9e3-3ea3-9947-1dc6ab6946ce-35395744653.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":10,"country":"US","yt":"LEHqOfKeabc","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/soul-ii-soul/club-classics-vol-one"},"desc":"When American urban-contemporary radio was bombarding its listeners with one Guy clone after another in the late '80s and early '90s, British neo-soulsters like Soul II Soul, Lisa Stansfield, and the Chimes offered highly creative and gutsy alternatives. With influences ranging from Chic to hip-hop to African music, Soul II Soul's debut album, Club Classics, Vol. 1 (titled Keep on Movin' in the U.S.), was among the most rewarding R&B releases of 1989. Soul II Soul leader/producer/composer Jazzie B takes one risk after another -- all of which pay off. The group enjoyed major hits with the Chic-influenced gems \"Keep ."},"artist_ref":{"id":66683307046377,"name":"Soul II Soul","info":{"img":null}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":136937573393074,"type":"genre","name":"hip hop","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1554,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":56177319906220,"type":"genre","name":"electronica","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":262,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":187404219874822,"type":"genre","name":"Deep House","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":247,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":211647710982479,"type":"genre","name":"Acid Jazz","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":236,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":111306765148197,"type":"genre","name":"dance","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":151,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":264824775713421,"type":"genre","name":"club","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":37,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":208090535551350,"type":"genre","name":"UK Street Soul","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":54